Negative control for each renderer carrying its OWN `uiTypeIs` tester (`R6-36`).

Points the icon renderer's tester at another member's ui type. The component is
untouched and still registered, so the registry still holds four entries — but
two of them now claim `TableCellText` and none claims `TableCellIcon`, which is
the copy-paste a fifth cell type invites. It is the tester, not the component,
that decides what a declaration draws, and this is the only line that says so.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the cell-renderer spec — a declared `TableCellIcon` element is claimed by
nothing and draws an empty cell, so the filled/outline glyph cases fail; the
text cases stay green, which is what makes the mutation a plausible mistake
rather than a switched-off feature.

